Another way: imagine writing the number on paper. 25 has two digits. When you multiply by 10, you're shifting all the digits one position to the left, so the 2 moves from the tens place to the hundreds place, and the 5 moves from the ones to the tens. Then, since there's nothing in the ones place, you put a zero there. Hence, 250.

